  What is En Primeur?
  
  "En Primeur" is a French term meaning "first" and it refers to the practice
  of buying wine while it is still in the barrel, some months (or even years)
  before it is bottled and shipped off to wine merchants.
  
  [Learn more](https://www.wine-searcher.com/en-primeur/guide "Lear more")
  
  1\. Purchase
  
  Customers get the chance to buy a wine at the earliest possible stage, usually a year or 18 months before release.
  
  2\. Allocation
  
  Customers secure an allocation of the wine, typically in case lots, rather than by individual bottles.
  
  3\. Maturation
  
  The wine continues to age in the barrel, at the winery.
  
  4\. Bottling and shipping
  
  Once the wine is deemed ready, it is bottled and shipped to the relevant wine merchants, who then divide up their allocations among their customers.
  
